31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Many potential members won't commit to a full year upfront. Also, mid-year joiners require tedious manual calculations.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The treasurer spent six hours a month chasing individual payments. Yearly collection is vastly more efficient.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It's worse than I thought. A quarter of us provide two-thirds of the attendance, and the same nine people do all the work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Door charges killed our weekday turnout. People stopped feeling like the club belonged to them.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,Seventy percent of our costs are fixed—hall hire and insurance. We pay these regardless of who shows up.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if costs are fixed, we can't rely solely on per-event fees without risking a deficit.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, but manual calculations for mid-year joiners and chasing small fees is a nightmare for the treasurer.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, but is it fair that the few of us doing the work and attending everything subsidize those who never come?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, if we make it too ""fair,"" we create a barrier. People are already hesitant to attend.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"We can't afford guesswork. If we don't cover those fixed costs upfront, the account will just keep thinning.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, I agree. We need to keep the entry barrier low so people can drift in.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests a system that minimizes labor. Chasing money is not a productive use of a volunteer's time.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I'm not asking for complexity, just a recognition that the burden isn't shared equally.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The moment you charge per event, you change the psychology from ""my club"" to ""a service I'm buying.""","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,But we have people asking for monthly payments because they can't afford the lump sum.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
