60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is too steep for newcomers. Option B might feel like a caste system. Option C is the most welcoming.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is a disaster for the treasurer. Option A is the only one that is administratively sustainable.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B allows us to balance the cost based on usage, which addresses the unfairness I found in the records.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is exactly what killed the weekday turnout. I cannot support it. Option A keeps the habit of attending.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A ensures our fixed costs are covered immediately. We can't risk the account running dry.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, but what about the people who can't pay all at once? They'll just not join.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, we can offer a payment plan, but the structure should be a flat fee to save the treasurer's sanity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, a flat fee just continues the trend of the active few subsidizing the inactive many.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the ""inactive many"" are the ones we need to encourage to come back.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,I agree with Benjamin. Stability first. We need a guaranteed sum to cover the hall and insurance.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I still worry that a high flat fee is a wall for new people.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Option B is just Option A with more paperwork. It's a logical fallacy to think it solves the workload.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If we go with A, we are ignoring the fact that some members never even show up.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'd rather have a member who rarely comes but feels welcome than a ""fair"" system that empties the room.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"We can't let the club fold because we were too worried about ""fairness"" to cover the rent.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I'll concede to A if we keep the figure reasonable.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A is the only rational choice for the staff.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I still prefer B, but I see the administrative argument.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,A is the best for the atmosphere.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,A is the only way to ensure we are solvent.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
